Implementation:
```js
function fold(text, { digraph = true } = {}) {
  let out = String(text ?? '').toLowerCase();
  if (digraph) out = out.replace(/ä/g,'ae').replace(/ö/g,'oe').replace(/ü/g,'ue').replace(/ß/g,'ss');
  out = out.normalize('NFD').replace(/\p{M}+/gu, ''); // strip remaining combining marks (è, é, à, ç…)
  return out;
}
export const foldSearch = (text) => fold(text, { digraph: true });
export const foldLoose = (text) => fold(text, { digraph: false });
```

Haystack: `titleText(record)` returns lowercase joined string. For matching I need both foldings; computing two normalizations per record per query would be wasteful for 169 records × tokens — that's fine actually (169 × cheap regex). But `filterRecords` runs on every keystroke over 169 records — still trivial. However cleaner: cache folded haystacks in a WeakMap keyed by record? Or export both `titleText` (raw) and folded variants. Let me keep `titleText` unchanged (other code may rely on the lowercase string) and add:

